@startuml
 title One drone control step: sensor input to movement command
 autonumber
 hide footbox
 skinparam shadowing false
 skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
 skinparam ParticipantPadding 22
 skinparam maxMessageSize 90

 participant "AirSim" as Sim
 participant "Environment\n(airsim_env.py)" as Env
 participant "Gym wrappers\n(DummyVecEnv + VecNormalize)" as Wrappers
 participant "PPO policy\n(run_progress_model.py)" as PPO
 participant "Feature extractor\n(customnetwork.py)" as Features

 == 1. Read the drone's current input ==
 Env -> Sim: getMultirotorState()\nrequest linear velocity
 Sim --> Env: velocity [vx, vy, vz] (m/s)
 Env -> Sim: simGetImages([ImageRequest(1, DepthVis, True)])
 Sim --> Env: float DepthVis pixels + image width/height
 Env -> Env: transform_input(osb=[responses, [vx, vy, vz]])
 note right of Env
 transform_input returns [image, velocity].
 Image processing: float32 pixels -> clip(255*3*pixel, 0, 255)
 -> uint8 -> reshape to camera height/width -> resize to (72,128)
 -> grayscale -> float32 / 255 -> image shape (1,72,128).
 Velocity remains a 3-value float32 vector [vx,vy,vz].
 end note

 == 2. Assemble the observation ==
 Env -> Env: obs_combine(img=image, vel=velocity)
 note right of Env
 obs_combine repeats [vx,vy,vz] across 72 rows,
 making (1,72,3), then appends it after the 128 image columns.
 Return shape: (1,72,131).
 end note
 Env -> Wrappers: observation
 Wrappers -> PPO: batched observation
 note right of Wrappers
 DummyVecEnv adds the batch dimension: (1,1,72,131).
 VecNormalize has norm_obs=False, so the values are unchanged.
 end note

 == 3. Turn the observation into an action ==
 PPO -> Features: model.predict(observation, deterministic=True)
 Features -> Features: feature_extractor.forward(obs)
 Features -> Features: obs_split(combined)
 note right of Features
 obs_split separates image (batch,1,72,128) from velocity (batch,3).
 It reads velocity from the last 3 columns of the first image row.
 CNN: conv1 -> conv2 -> conv3 -> flatten to 256 -> image_fc1 64
 -> LeakyReLU -> image_fc2 48.
 Velocity branch: vel_fc1 maps 3 -> 48.
 Join both 48-value branches -> Tanh -> 96 features.
 end note
 Features --> PPO: 96 features
 PPO -> PPO: Actor MLP 96 -> 128 -> 64 -> 32 -> 16
 PPO -> PPO: action head produces 3 Gaussian means
 PPO --> Wrappers: action array (1,3) = [x,y,z]
 note right of PPO
 deterministic=True uses the distribution mean; each action
 component is clipped to [-1,1]. The critic is not used by predict().
 end note

 == 4. Send the movement command ==
 Wrappers -> Env: step(action[0]) = step([x,y,z])
 Env -> Env: AirSimEnv_Progress.step(action)\nthen AirSimEnvBase.step(quad_offset=action)
 Env -> Sim: moveByVelocityAsync(1.5*x, 1.5*y+0.5,\n1.5*z, step_duration=0.5).join()
 Sim --> Env: movement completes
 Env --> Wrappers: next observation, reward, done, info
 Wrappers --> PPO: next observation is used on the next step

@enduml